  "content": "## Claim\n\nFor arbitrary reducers with attribution requirements, CRDTs and operational transformation fall short:\n\n- **CRDTs** require commutative ops and cannot express state-dependent validation (e.g. balance checks)\n- **OT** transforms/rewrites operations to preserve intent, breaking append-only auditability\n\n**Operational reshuffle** (Powerhouse) keeps actions immutable; only ordering and replayed result hashes change when streams merge.\n\n## Why provenance cares\n\nIf operations are rewritten, authorship and mechanism trails become unstable. Immutable actions keep the audit surface intact under concurrency.",
